Adds the Stellux nvkmd's exec ctx over one queue of the dev's context. A
batch of waits, pushes and signals goes to the kernel in one GPU_SUBMIT,
or past the call's limits of 32 points and 4096 command ranges in a chain
of them. Each submission signals the ctx's private timeline and each later
part of a chain waits on the point before it, so a failed part fails the
rest. The device check reads each ctx's private timeline, so failed work
loses the device, since Vulkan reports failed work only as device loss. A
full queue makes the submit wait for its oldest submission and retry once.

